      "content": "The Eurostar, when traveling from London to Paris, generally has luggage allowances that are quite generous, but you should always double-check the official Eurostar website for the most current specifics for your ticket class. For general guidance, most passengers are allowed a certain number of pieces, and while specific weight limits can vary, they are usually quite high for standard checked baggage. I recommend aiming to be at St Pancras well in advance, perhaps 60 to 90 minutes before departure, especially if you have heavy bags that might require extra time at the check-in desk. This buffer time is crucial to avoid any last-minute stress!",
